==Yoruba==

===Etymology 1===
Proposed to be derived from {{inh|yo|alv-yor-pro|*o-ríɣo}}, {{m|alv-yor-pro|*o-rí}}, from {{inh|yo|alv-edk-pro|*o-ríɣo}}, {{m|alv-edk-pro|*o-rí}}, ultimately from {{inh|yo|alv-yrd-pro|*ó-ɗí}}, {{m|alv-yrd-pro|*ó-rí}}. Cognate with {{cog|igl|ójí}}. The compounding of the suffix "ɣo" (later "wo") is possibly an Proto-Edekiri innovation still maintained in a majority of Edekiri languages, and the non-suffixed version likely existed side by side. However, {{cog|aye|ago}} may suggest it is a remnant of an older root. See potential non-Yoruboid cognates, {{cog|aqg|egírí|igíri}}, {{cog|bnt-pro|*mʊ̀tʊ́è}}, {{cog|nic-grf-pro|*tú}}, {{cog|nic-plt-pro|*-tii}}, {{cog|nic-bco-pro|*-to}}, possibly {{cog|ig|isi}}, {{cog|ibe|ìcùm}}, perhaps ultimately from {{inh|yo|alv-pro|*-li-}} or {{inh|yo|nic-pro|*-túi}}, {{m|nic-pro|*-tu}}

Cognate with {{cog|idd|erío}}, {{cog|ife|eríwo}}, {{cog|ulb|órí}}, and {{cog|its|orígho}}. Folk etymologies often attribute etymology to {{af|yo|o-|rí|t1=nominalizing prefix|id1=nominalizing prefix|t2=to see}}

====Pronunciation====
*{{yo-IPA|orí}}

====Noun====
{{yo-noun|orí}}

# [[head]], [[top]], [[leader]]
# {{lb|yo|Yoruba religion}} the [[metaphysical]] [[concept]] of one's [[spiritual]] [[intuition]], [[destiny]], and [[consciousness]], deified as a divinity, {{l|yo|Orí}}.

